{"`if client_sample_rate:` evaluates to `False` when `client_sample_rate` is `0` or `0.0`, silently skipping the `sample_rate` assignment for events with a zero sample rate. Should use an explicit `None` check instead.": 0.7007732391357422, "`hash(tuple(sorted(snuba_params.project_ids)))` is not safe for external cache keys because Python's `hash()` for tuples is randomized per-process by default (`PYTHONHASHSEED`), causing different workers to produce different hash values for the same project IDs and making caching ineffective.": 0.9451007843017578, "The new `upsampled_count` definition is dead code because a later definition in the same list silently overwrites it due to dictionary comprehension. Either remove the duplicate and update the existing definition, or remove the existing one - but the existing `ifNull(sample_weight, 1)` fallback is safer for handling NULL values.": 0.3539108335971832, "Test asserts upsampling is applied (`count == 10`) when only one of two queried projects is allowlisted, but `_are_all_projects_error_upsampled` uses `all()` which returns `False` unless every queried project is in the allowlist. The expected value should be `1` to match actual behavior, or the test intent needs reconsideration.": 0.25098323822021484}